{"type":"text","timestamp":1787404104967,"sessionID":"ses_fd66ca4b9ffehsWVNuNYsifl3c","part":{"id":"prt_029962a1e001JwXNLdR15sXYRc","messageID":"msg_029960b2c001kKiCntf787nBnI","sessionID":"ses_fd66ca4b9ffehsWVNuNYsifl3c","type":"text","text":"All requirements verified and no regressions. Summary of changes in `lib/glob-match.js`:\n\n- **`ignore`** (string or array): an input that matches the pattern but also matches an ignore pattern is excluded (`isMatch` becomes `false`). Evaluated via a separate `globMatch(ignore, …)` call with callbacks/`ignore` stripped from its options, so it doesn't inherit the caller's own hooks.\n- **`onResult`** fires once per input (match, ignore, or non-match) with a result object carrying `glob`, `regex`, `input`, `output`, and the final `isMatch`.\n- **`onMatch`** fires only for inputs that end up matching.\n- **`onIgnore`** fires only for inputs excluded by an ignore pattern.\n- An input that never matched the pattern is reported as a non-match (`isMatch: false`) and never triggers `onIgnore`.\n- When no hooks/ignore are supplied, the original matcher (including array patterns and the `returnObject` form) is returned unchanged, preserving existing behaviour.","time":{"start":1787404102174,"end":1787404104963}}}
